      "description": "Human Resources | Offices & Services | Methodist University Skip Main Navigation Skip to site alert Secondary Apply Request Info Visit Giving Methodist University Menu Secondary Apply Request Info Visit Giving For You Close For You Prospective Students Newly Admitted Students Current Students Online Students Military & Veteran Students International Students Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni Menu Search You are here: Home Offices & Services Human Resources Human Resources Human Resources Explore This Section Close Human Resources Positions Available Student Employment Title IX Volunteers at MU Human Resources manages the employee information of Methodist University and is located in the Horner Administration Building. Prospective Employees To apply for a position, go to the Positions Available page and click on the job posting. At the bottom of the posting, you will see a button to apply. Current Employees Employee Information Employee Handbook (Revised February 2025) 2025-26 Hourly Pay Schedule 2025-26 Exempt (Salaried) Pay Schedule 2026 Holiday Schedule Methodist University Rapid Response Fund (MURRF) Employee Benefits 2026 Employee Benefits Guide Employee Assistance Program Discounts with MU ID Employment Verification For all verifications of employment, please contact Human Resources at [email protected] . Access to 1095-C Forms Due to the Paperwork Reduction Act and the Employer Reporting Improvement Act passed by Congress and signed into law in December 2024, Methodist University is following the Paperwork Reduction Act that amends the ACA by no longer requiring employers to send physical copies of 1095-C Forms to the employees and former employees. All employees will receive an email notification from BenefitFirst stating the 1095-C Form is available on their website. To retrieve your 1095-C form online, please adhere to the following instructions: Access the employee portal at benefitfirst.com On the Home Screen, click tab in upper right hand corner labeled “My 1095” Should you have any inquiries and require assistance in accessing your 1095-C, please contact Kathy Allan, Employee Benefits Specialist, at [email protected] . Human Resources Staff Debra Yeatts, MBA Chief Human Resources Officer Contact Email: [email protected] Phone: 910.630.7385 Department Human Resources Jennifer Dumond, B.S. Deputy Chief Human Resources Officer Contact Email: [email protected] Phone: 910.630.7255 Department Human Resources Holly VanDresar, M.B.A., PHR Senior Human Resources Generalist Contact Email: [email protected] Phone: 910.630.7613 Department Human Resources Stephanie McLeod, M.S.M. Senior Human Resources Generalist, School of Medicine Contact Email: [email protected] Department Human Resources | School of Medicine | College of Medicine Sunny Harrison Student Employment Coordinator Contact Email: [email protected] Department Human Resources Methodist University Location 5400 Ramsey Street Fayetteville, NC 28311 910.630.7000 Helpful Links Maps & Directions Parking Information Emergency Information Employment News Event Calendar Connect With Us Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Title IX Consumer Information © Methodist University 2026 Site Menu Search Submit Site Explore MU In Brief In Our Own Words In Pictures In the World In Athletics In Our Local Community In the Numbers Our Value On a Tour About MU About Our Relationship to the United Methodist Church A Brief History of Methodist University The Arts at MU Offices & Services Our Mission Strategic Initiatives Careers at MU Accreditation Event Rentals Leadership Academics Academic Programs (On-Campus & Online) Methodist University Online Davis Memorial Library One Stop Academic Calendars & Schedules Academic Catalog Registrar Graduation Educational Centers Faculty & Staff Awards Admissions & Aid Apply Request Information Visit Campus First-Year Students Transfer Students International Studen